From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:09:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 175/194] hjviewer: a download checks the PC's file names,
 folders and the overwrite answer on this device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The controller trusted what the PC sent during a download. A modified PC
could list a file under a name such as "..\x" or an absolute path, name
an "empty folder" outside the folder being fetched, or send a file's
blocks after the question "overwrite?" was answered with no or not asked
at all, and the controller wrote where the PC said: outside the folder
the user chose, or over an existing file. The controller now checks all
of it itself: the names of a remote folder listing by the PC's naming
rules, the name being downloaded before anything is sent, every
empty-folder path against the chosen folder (and no link on the way),
the destination and its .download/.digest staging names for links, and
it writes over an existing file or a stale staging file only for the
file the user (or the remembered answer) approved. A refused download
ends as an error instead of being printed to the log. Uploads to the PC
and the PC's own code do not change.

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk b44b71cfabe9898d5eada9b07cb583fe995ed45e (Fix/download path validation (#16601))
Against upstream's diff:
- file_model.dart: the import hunk added by hand (our import list
  differs); the other hunks as upstream.
- native_model.dart: PlatformFFI.setBindingForTesting, the two-line test
  hook upstream's Flutter test needs. Upstream added it with its keyboard
  shortcuts feature (074006386), which we do not have; nothing else of
  that commit is taken.
- Korean texts. Upstream's new errors are English and neither upstream's
  nor our file screens showed a job's error text, only "오류". Our screens
  now say why this device refused a transfer: HjvFileTexts.refused maps
  the errors to a few words ("저장할 수 없는 파일 이름", "폴더 경로가
  올바르지 않음", "받는 폴더에 링크가 있음", "같은 이름의 파일이 이미
  있음", "이어받을 파일이 맞지 않음", "원격에서 파일 목록을 바꿈"; English
  where the app is English), the desktop job card shows them after "오류"
  and the phone's sheet under "오류!". The sheet's texts now take the
  width its buttons leave and end in an ellipsis. Any other error stays
  the bare word as before.
- Tests: upstream's Rust tests unchanged; upstream's Flutter test also
  checks the Korean reason of each refusal and that the phone's sheet
  fits it at 320 px and 130 % text; hjviewer_session_look_test.dart
  holds the mapping.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
